-- title:
--   Degree of the first degeneracy embedding over X₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $M$ be a natural number with $M \neq 0$, and let $q$ be a natural number that is prime. Consider the two intermediate fields of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by base change along the coefficientwise embedding $L$-linearly: `laurentBaseChange L F₀` is the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image of $F₀ \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ under `coeffEmb L`. Take $F₀$ to be, first, the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionField M` $=$ `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ M` of level $\Gamma_1(M)$, and second, `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M (M * q)`, the $q$-expansion function field of the group $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(Mq)$. The map `heckeAlphaOneBar L M q` is the inclusion of the first of these base-changed fields into the second, as an $L$-algebra homomorphism. The assertion is that the rank of the larger field as a module over the smaller one, via the algebra structure induced by this inclusion, equals $q$ if $q \mid M$ and $q+1$ otherwise; in particular this rank is finite.
--
--   This is the degree of the first degeneracy covering $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(Mq)) \to X_1(M)$, equivalently the index $[\Gamma_1(M) : \Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(Mq)] = [\Gamma_0(M) : \Gamma_0(Mq)]$, computed on the level of function fields after base change to $L$. It feeds the construction and the degeneracy relations for the Hecke operators $T_q$ and $U_q$ on $J_1$, and is used in the comparison of Hecke correspondences with the operators on $X_1$ and in spanning arguments for the Hecke roof.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrankAlong_heckeAlphaOneBar.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1HeckeOperator

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.finrankAlong_heckeAlphaOneBar (L : Type*) [Field L] [Algebra ℚ L]
    (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime] :
    AlgebraicCurve.finrankAlong L (ModularCurve.heckeAlphaOneBar L M q) =
      if q ∣ M then q else q + 1 := by sorry
